        rules: {
          objective: 'Make the lowest possible five-card hand. Win the pot at showdown.',
          gameplay: 'Five cards each; betting then draw (discard and replace), betting, draw, betting, draw, betting, showdown. Three draws; stand pat or draw 0-5 cards each time.',
          keyRules: [
            'Low hand wins',
            'Straights and flushes are bad',
            'Aces high',
            'Best hand: 7-5-4-3-2 offsuit',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Play tight: start with hands that have a deuce and a seven, or three cards to an eight that don’t make a straight. Never draw to hands that can make a straight. A-2-3-4-5 is bad (ace is high). Best hand is 7-5-4-3-2 offsuit.',
          intermediate: 'Position matters: act last when possible to see opponents’ draw sizes. Be aggressive—bet and raise more than you check and call. From early position raise only with strong two-card draws (e.g. 2-3-4, 2-3-7); loosen in late position.',
          advanced: 'Snowing: in position, stand pat with weak hands when opponents have drawn many cards to pressure them. On the final draw, jack-high is slightly favoured over a one-card draw; adjust by position. Avoid drawing to nine-lows when inexperienced.',
          tips: [
            'Best hand is 7-5-4-3-2 (no flush, no straight); aces are always high.',
            'Starting hands: need a deuce and seven or three to an eight; avoid straight draws.',
            'Snowing (standing pat with a bluff) works when opponents have drawn and you act last.',
            'Position is critical—see how many cards opponents draw before deciding.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
